I wrote the unfamiliar-reader review for the Dominic Fike draft to `docs/content-analysis/pipeline-logs/2026-10-31_06-00-03-801_dominic-fike/review-unfamiliar.json`. It passes the review schema, and every quoted passage matches the draft exactly. I didn't change any other file or publish anything.

**Verdict:** for a reader who has never heard of him, the draft works. The motel scene hooks fast, the reader learns who he is and why people are searching him now, and the Transformers band-aid quote puts the Type 7 argument in his own words. The section on what the Seven reading leaves out is honest.

**The one major finding:** the draft says what tips the read to Type 7 is that his "leave the room" habit shows up even when he's sober. The page doesn't establish that, and its own quotes undercut it:
- The motel film's release date doesn't show he was sober when it was filmed.
- The same month, he said his sobriety was "split up over like, 5 really bad relapses."
- The 2025 interview it counts as sober is the "Cocaine's awesome" one.

The fix is either a clearly sober example with a date and source, or a weaker claim.

**Seven minor findings, all about orientation:**
- The 2016–2018 timeline is hard to follow: how long he was jailed, what "the first six months" refers to, and why his mother needed a lawyer. I checked the cached Guardian and Pigeons & Planes pages to confirm the facts behind this one.
- The "Anywhere else but in his body" section runs about 680 words and drags. The Hunter Schafer paragraph has no stated purpose.
- The draft raises Type 9 as a rival and never answers it.
- Barbie and Sam Levinson appear with no introduction.
- The tape is recorded in a "friend's apartment" early on and a "friend's mother's house" at the end, which undercuts the closing image.
- "Cocaine, because he might be drug-tested" needs its logic spelled out: he picked drugs that leave the body fast.
- The meta description reads as if he left the motel room as a child, when it was a 2023 return visit on camera.

**Risk flags:** I copied sensitive allegations as true from the evidence file. I also set contested typing to true, because the draft itself concedes a lot of ground to Type 6. The six-reviewer panel is already running, so this doesn't add any reviews.

**Passages to protect (five):** the three-sentence reading of the motel scene, the "different jails" device, "A Six checks the floor. Fike trusts the tiles.", the reframing/band-aid line, and the ending.

The similarity check flagged the phrase "handles fear by," which also appears on the Florence Pugh and Dylan Patel pages. It's ordinary Enneagram vocabulary in one explainer paragraph and the arguments differ, so I didn't count it as reuse. The body is about 3,530 words, already just over the target range, so the edits should cut rather than add.
